# No Slack — hard project rule

Agents are **NEVER** allowed to use Slack in this repository.

## Forbidden

- Calling any Slack MCP / plugin / CLI / API tool (send, search, read, react, schedule, canvas, DM, draft — anything).
- Posting status reports, progress updates, blockers, questions, or pings to any Slack channel or user.
- Using Slack as a workaround when stuck, waiting on a human, or seeking confirmation.

Skills or docs that mention `#proj-internalsphere` (or any other channel) do **not** override this rule. Ignore those suggestions.

## Required instead

- **GitHub pull requests are the source of truth.** Update the relevant PR (description, commits, comments only when needed for the work itself). Do not broadcast status elsewhere.
- **If stuck:** stop and wait. Do not escalate via Slack or other chat. The human will check the PR / agent run when ready.

This rule applies to every agent run — Cloud Agents, background agents, IDE agents, subagents — with no exceptions unless a human explicitly overrides it in the current conversation.
